{"name":"Velvet Cosmos","hex":"#441144","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"velvet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A closely woven fabric (originally of silk, now also of cotton or man-made fibres) with a thick short pile on one side.","Very fine fur, including the skin and fur on a deer's antlers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with velvet or with a covering of a similar texture.","To coat raw meat in starch, then in oil, preparatory to frying."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/velvet"},{"term":"cosmos","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The universe regarded as a system with harmony and order.\n\n A harmonious, ordered whole.","A harmonious, ordered whole."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various mostly Mexican herbs of the genus Cosmos having radiate heads of variously coloured flowers and pinnate leaves."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cosmos"}],"entries":[{"title":"Velvet","blocks":[{"text":"Velvet is a type of woven fabric with a dense, even pile that gives it a distinctive soft feel. Historically, velvet was typically made from silk. Modern velvet can be made from silk, linen, cotton, wool, synthetic fibers, silk-cotton blends, or synthetic-natural fiber blends."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Blue_velvet_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Blue_velvet_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Velvet"},{"title":"Cosmos","blocks":[{"text":"The cosmos is an alternative name for the universe or its nature or order. Usage of the word cosmos implies viewing the universe as a complex and orderly system or entity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/The_Nights_Long_Moments_%28152181573%29.jpeg/330px-The_Nights_Long_Moments_%28152181573%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://e